    <h1>Kiavi Fix-and-Flip Loans, Explained</h1>
    <p class="lede">Kiavi is the largest fix-and-flip lender in the country — $5.5B originated in 2024. Here's exactly what its bridge loan looks like and how to size one for your deal.</p>

    <h2>Terms at a glance</h2>
    <div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Loan size</td><td>~$100K–$3M</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Term</td><td>12, 18, or 24 months, interest-only</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Rates</td><td>~7.75%–12% depending on experience, leverage, credit (<a href="/kiavi-rates/">rate guide</a>)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Leverage</td><td>Up to <strong>95% of purchase + rehab costs (LTC)</strong> and <strong>80% of ARV</strong>; 100% of rehab budget financed</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Income docs</td><td>None — no W-2s, tax returns, or DTI</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Speed</td><td>Closings in as little as 7–10 business days</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Prepayment penalty</td><td>Generally none on bridge loans</td></tr>
      </tbody>
