    <h2>How the loan is sized</h2>
    <p>Kiavi lends against two ceilings and your loan is capped by whichever binds first: <strong>loan-to-cost</strong> (up to 95% of purchase price + rehab budget) and <strong>after-repair value</strong> (total loan up to 80% of ARV). The rehab budget is held back and released in <strong>draws</strong> as work completes — you front each stage, submit photos/inspection through the dashboard, and get reimbursed. Run your numbers in our <a href="/kiavi-deal-calculator/">deal calculator</a>, which applies both ceilings and the 70% rule side by side.</p>

    {% include "partials/cta.njk" %}

    <h2>Experience tiers</h2>
    <p>Kiavi prices by your verified exits in the last 24 months: 0 exits qualifies but pays the most; 1–4 exits sits mid-range; <strong>5+ exits unlocks floor pricing and maximum leverage</strong>. Exits at other lenders count — document them. First flip? You're eligible; just budget for the higher tier and see <a href="/kiavi-requirements/">the full requirements</a>.</p>

    <h2>What flippers should watch</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Interest accrues on drawn funds</strong> — a realistic rehab timeline matters more than a perfect one.</li>
      <li><strong>ARV discipline.</strong> Kiavi's valuation model will check your ARV; use the <a href="/faqs/what-is-kiavi-arv-estimator/">ARV estimator</a> before you offer, not after.</li>
      <li><strong>Exit flexibility.</strong> If the flip becomes a keeper, Kiavi's <a href="/kiavi-dscr-loans/">DSCR refinance</a> is the in-house exit — no new lender hunt mid-project.</li>
    </ul>

